description:
AI voice calls to customers whose laundry order is ready, and the WhatsApp confirmation of what was agreed on the call. One row per outbound call. Flow: (1) a production order completes (alertDispatcher.notify_cycle_done) for a company with voice calls enabled -> POST /voiceCalls/place resolves the order's client and phone server-side, mints a signed call token (VOICE_CALL_SECRET, HMAC; format and payload in LoanAgents_SmartLoans voice/call_token.py) and asks Twilio to dial with TwiML <Connect><Stream url=wss://loanagents-smartloans.azurewebsites.net/voice/twilio-stream> carrying the token as a <Parameter>; (2) the LoanAgents voice secretary (Gemini Live) talks with the customer and PROPOSES a PICKUP_AGREEMENT -- it never writes; (3) LoanAgents POSTs the call result to /voiceCalls/result (worker key); (4) if there is an agreement, the backend sends the approved Meta template acuerdo_llamada with the summary to the client's WhatsApp and stores it as the pending proposal of that WhatsApp conversation (whatsappChannels.set_pending, same mechanism as CREATE_RESERVATION); (5) the customer's deterministic 'si' (posSupportChat._classify_confirmation, existing) confirms it: the agreement is marked confirmed and staff get a push. Never auto-confirm: an agreement is only confirmed by the customer's own WhatsApp reply. Non-custodial: nothing here moves or records money -- paymentMethod is only how the customer plans to pay. CONSTRAINTS: (a) walk-in client 1 (WALK_IN_CLIENT_ID, the 'mostrador' placeholder with a real phone on file) is never called; (b) the client's phone comes only from clients.cellphone of the order's client -- never from the request; (c) idempotent per orderId: one call per order, a second place request returns the existing row; (d) calls only inside the company's calling window (default 09:00-20:00 America/Hermosillo, UTC-7 no DST) and never when clientContactPreferences opts the client out of calls; (e) feature flag per company (VOICE_CALLS_ENABLED_COMPANIES, empty = off) -- customer calling stays OFF until the voice acceptance criteria pass; (f) only the LATEST agreementRevision of a call can be confirmed: a 'si' to an older revision is rejected and the newest summary is re-sent; (g) the agreement is validated again server-side, independently of the AI: date within the next 8 days and inside that weekday's reservationHours, time not already passed, deliveryMode 'delivery' only when businessInfo.deliveryPolicy is registered, paymentMethod (if any) among businessInfo.paymentMethods when they are registered -- an invalid agreement is not sent, the call is marked needs_staff and staff get a push; (h) caller ID: TWILIO_VOICE_CALLER_ID must be a Twilio-owned Mexican number -- a verified non-Twilio Mexican caller ID was dropped by the carrier on a real test (2026-11-07); (i) no transcript, phone or address is ever written to the log tables (observability redactor) -- the agreement JSON is stored on this row only. OPEN QUESTIONS: what 'confirmed' should change in productionOrders (e.g. a pickupAt column) is left to a follow-up PRD; this module only records and confirms the agreement. INTEGRATIONS: Twilio Programmable Voice (Calls.create, status callback) -- reuse TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID/TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN already in the backend; Meta WhatsApp Cloud API template acuerdo_llamada (Utility, es_MX) -- must be submitted and approved in Meta Business Manager before go-live; text and samples to add to docs/whatsapp-templates.md; LoanAgents_SmartLoans /voice/twilio-stream (WebSocket) -- shares VOICE_CALL_SECRET. WHATSAPP TEMPLATE acuerdo_llamada (UTILITY, es_MX), body: "📞 *Resumen de tu llamada - {{1}}*

Hola *{{2}}*, esto acordamos:

🧺 *Entrega:* {{3}}
📅 *Fecha:* {{4}}
🕐 *Hora:* {{5}}
📝 *Notas:* {{6}}

Responde *SÍ* para confirmar o escríbenos si quieres cambiar algo."; samples {1}..{6}: Lavandería GMO, Gilberto, Recoger en sucursal, domingo 8 de noviembre, 12:00, Pago en efectivo. OBSERVABILITY: workflow_step for order_ready -> call_placed -> call_answered -> agreement_proposed -> whatsapp_sent -> confirmed (one workflowId per orderId); timed_integration around Twilio and Meta calls; log_audit on agreementStatus changes. Never log phone, address or transcript. BACKEND CONVENTIONS (reviewer-enforced): routes_/voiceCall.py declares router = APIRouter() with NO prefix and NO tags, and every decorator carries its full path exactly as listed in backend.endpoints (/voiceCalls, /all_voiceCalls, /one_voiceCalls, /voiceCalls/place, /voiceCalls/twilio-status, /voiceCalls/result, /voiceCalls/confirm); route files never import HTTPException -- connectors return JSONResponse with the status code; all HTTP calls (Twilio REST Calls.json, Meta Graph) use httpx.AsyncClient, not the twilio SDK; validate X-Twilio-Signature with hmac/hashlib (HMAC-SHA1 of URL + sorted form params, base64) instead of twilio.request_validator.
